        "id": "2995",
        "question": "$ABCDEFGH$ shown below is a right rectangular prism.  If the volume of pyramid $ABCH$ is 20, then what is the volume of $ABCDEFGH$?\n\n<image1>",
        "options": [],
        "image": "images/2995.jpg",
        "decoded_image": {
          "path": "images/2995.jpg",
          "original_path": "2995.jpg"
        },
        "answer": "120",
        "solution": "We add the edges of the pyramid to our diagram below.\n\n[asy]\nimport three;\ntriple A,B,C,D,EE,F,G,H;\nA = (0,0,0);\nB = (5,0,0);\nC = (5,6,0);\nD= (0,6,0);\nEE = (0,0,4);\nF = B+EE;\nG = C + EE;\nH = D + EE;\ndraw(B--C--D);\ndraw(B--A--D,dashed);\ndraw(EE--F--G--H--EE);\ndraw(B--H--A--EE,dashed);\ndraw(A--C,dashed);\ndraw(B--F);\ndraw(C--G);\ndraw(D--H--C);\nlabel(\"$A$\",A,SSW);\nlabel(\"$B$\",B,W);\nlabel(\"$C$\",C,S);\nlabel(\"$D$\",D,E);\nlabel(\"$E$\",EE,N);\nlabel(\"$F$\",F,W);\nlabel(\"$G$\",G,SW);\nlabel(\"$H$\",H,E);\n[/asy]\n\nTaking $ABC$ to be the base of pyramid $ABCH$, the height is $HD$.  Therefore, the volume of pyramid $ABCH$ is $$\\frac{[ABC](HD)}{3}.$$We are given that this volume equals 20, so we have \\[{[ABC]\\cdot HD}=60.\\]The volume of prism $ABCDEFGH$ is the product of area of $ABCD$ and the height of the prism, which equals $HD$.   The area of $ABC$ is half the area of rectangle $ABCD$, so we have  \\begin{align*}\n\\text{Volume of }ABCDEFGH &= ([ABCD])(HD) \\\\\n&= 2([ABC])(HD) \\\\\n&= \\boxed{120}.\\end{align*}",
        "level": 2,
        "subject": "solid geometry"
      },
